<title>USA: FSA qualifies 14 muni bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies 14 muni bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said Tuesday it qualified for bond insurance the following 14 municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--San Francisco Airports, Calif., $275 million revenue bonds.</p>
<p>--North Brandford, Conn., $9.6 million general obligation bonds.  </p>
<p>--River Forest, Ill, $6 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Garden City, Kan., $2.11 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Delhi Township, Mich., $1 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Delhi Township, Mich., $1.945 million special assessment bonds.</p>
<p>--Sauk Rapids, Minn., $1.08 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Hoke County, N.C., $4.38 million refunding bonds.</p>
<p>--Onslow County, N.C., $1.2 million public improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Onslow County, N.C., $20 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Clark County, Nev., $7.2 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Newport School District, Pa., $4.84 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Grapevine, Texas, $2.92 million water and sewer bonds.</p>
<p>--Grapevine, Texas, $9.785 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
